From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:49:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(miniwin): release the IDirect3DMiniwin reference
 CreateDeviceFromSurface takes

Direct3DRMImpl::CreateDeviceFromSurface queried IID_IDirect3DMiniwin on the
DirectDraw object, which adds a reference, and never released it, whether
the renderer was created or not. The DirectDraw object then outlived its
last Release, so a client that sets the display up again after a failed
attempt (a 3D device that cannot claim the window) leaked one DirectDraw
object per attempt. The renderer reads the settings it needs while it is
created, so the reference is released straight after.

diff --git a/miniwin/src/d3drm/d3drm.cpp b/miniwin/src/d3drm/d3drm.cpp
index 677f299..38ffa25 100644
--- a/miniwin/src/d3drm/d3drm.cpp
+++ b/miniwin/src/d3drm/d3drm.cpp
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@ HRESULT Direct3DRMImpl::CreateDeviceFromSurface(
 	SDL_assert(miniwind3d);
 
 	DDRenderer = CreateDirect3DRMRenderer(miniwind3d, DDSDesc, guid);
+	// The renderer reads the settings it needs while it is created; the reference
+	// QueryInterface took would otherwise keep the DirectDraw object alive for good.
+	miniwind3d->Release();
 	if (!DDRenderer) {
 		SDL_LogError(SDL_LOG_CATEGORY_APPLICATION, "Failed to create a renderer for the selected device GUID");
 		return E_NOINTERFACE;
